The MistralClient class is internal and sealed, so it is not accessible from a test project outside its assembly. To test the logging call, we need to create a test class inside the same namespace and assembly or use InternalsVisibleTo attribute if available. Since we cannot modify the assembly attributes, let's create a test class inside the same namespace and mark it as internal to access the internal class.

I will submit a test class inside the Microsoft.SemanticKernel.Connectors.MistralAI.Client namespace to test the logging call. It will use Moq to verify the LogDebug call.

